## Does California Lemon Law Apply to Used Vehicles?

Yes, California lemon law does apply to used vehicles, but certain conditions must be met.

## Dealership Warranty

Many California car dealerships provide limited warranties on used vehicles, typically covering either the first 30 days after purchase or the first 1,000 miles - whichever comes first. If your used vehicle develops significant mechanical issues during this period and the defect meets the criteria under lemon law in California, you may be eligible to file a claim.

Your Rights as a Consumer

Car dealers are legally obligated to pay for your repairs or provide a buyback option if the vehicle qualifies as a lemon. All legal expenses are paid for by the warrantor.

Whether You Bought the Vehicle As-Is

By purchasing a vehicle “as-is”, you assume full responsibility for any defects or issues. In most cases, “as-is” purchases aren’t covered under California lemon law. However, the dealership must clearly disclose the “as-is” status in the buyer’s guide while the vehicle is on display. If this is missing, you may still have grounds for a claim.

